Source landscape is broad and mixed for Abiy Ahmed in Ethiopia in 2023: the strongest clusters are electoral-law and election-administration records, human-rights and press-freedom reporting, state-of-emergency material, and a smaller set of academic/legal overviews. I found more than 30 distinct candidate documents and preserved both favorable and adverse families, including official state sources, domestic observation reports, UN/regional materials, NGO reports, and local/international news. Search coverage is saturated enough for discovery, but later evidence work should still inspect the most relevant candidates directly.

